  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Vestronidase alfa may interact with CD276 antigen through a series of molecular targets. The drug is predicted to target IGROV-1, which is in turn targeted by Chondrosterin A or Chrysanthemic Acid, ethyl ester, both of which have a known target of CD276 antigen. Additionally, Vestronidase alfa is also predicted to interact with Free fatty acid receptor 2, which is targeted by a compound that also affects CD276 antigen. These findings collectively indicate that Vestronidase alfa may exert its biological effects through multiple pathways, potentially involving different molecular targets that ultimately converge on CD276 antigen. The evidence supports a complex, multi-target mechanism by which Vestronidase alfa could influence CD276 antigen, though the exact nature of the interactions and their functional significance remain to be fully elucidated.",
